{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Lineage_claims</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"neural_nets_lib","href":"../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Lineage_claims","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>The claim helpers of the lineage-refusal tests (gh-ocannl-1724, gh-ocannl-1744, gh-ocannl-1781): a refusal's text, an accepted call, an exact readback, a tensor's gradient node and a substring test. Six tests carried their own copies, one of them without the stderr echo of the refusal.</p><p>Call them qualified, through an alias (<code>module LC = Lineage_claims</code>, then <code>LC.refusal ...</code>), never under an <code>open</code>: past an open of a module <code>Verdict_callee</code> cannot read, a test's unqualified <code>p</code> reaches <code>Verdict</code> only ambiguously.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-grad_of\"><a href=\"#val-grad_of\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> grad_of : <span><a href=\"../Ocannl_tensor/Tensor/index.html#type-t\">Ocannl.Tensor.t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <a href=\"../Ocannl_tensor/Tensor/index.html#type-tn\">Ocannl.Tensor.tn</a></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The gradient node of a differentiable tensor; raises on a tensor without one.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-has\"><a href=\"#val-has\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> has : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> bool</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Whether <code>msg</code> contains <code>substring</code>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-exact\"><a href=\"#val-exact\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> exact : \u000A  <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base__Float</span>.t <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Array.t</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base__Float</span>.t <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Array.t</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>A readback equal to <code>want</code> cell for cell.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-refusal\"><a href=\"#val-refusal\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> refusal : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span>(<span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>)</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The text of the <code>User_error</code> <code>f</code> raises, echoed to stderr outside the golden; a failed claim when it raises none.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-accepted\"><a href=\"#val-accepted\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> accepted : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span>(<span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>)</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"type-var\">'a</span> option</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>Some</code> of what <code>f</code> returns, with a passing claim; a failed claim naming the refusal, and <code>None</code>, when it raises a <code>User_error</code>.</p></div></div>"}